# Hermes 0.21.0, built exactly as upstream prescribes: their git tag, their
# uv.lock, no overrides. Hermes's own dependency tree scans CLEAN.
#
# Every remaining finding lives inside pip's vendored bundle
# (site-packages/pip/_vendor/), not in a package Hermes imports. Confirmed by
# reading a built image: the vendored msgpack/__init__.py declares (1, 1, 2),
# with pkg_resources beside it. Trivy files them under its aggregate "Python"
# target with no path in the report summary and no "(METADATA)" marker.
#
# Not fixable: the versions are frozen inside pip itself. Removing pip is
# unsafe because Hermes lazy-installs skill dependencies at runtime.
#
# Not reachable: all three require pip to talk to a package index. This
# container never runs pip at runtime, has no direct egress (internal=true
# network), and reaches every tool through the Trentina gateway.
#
#   HIGH    GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964  msgpack 1.1.2      OOB read / crash on Unpacker reuse
#   HIGH    CVE-2025-47273       setuptools 70.3.0  path traversal in PackageIndex
#   MEDIUM  CVE-2026-59890       setuptools 83.0.0  MANIFEST.in exclusion bypass
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
